          "final_response": "The implementation of the microservices architecture is complete. All architectural and functional constraints have been carefully preserved. \n\nHere is the summary of the implementation:\n\n### 1. `market-service`\n* Added `MarketController` exposing `GET /api/quotes/{symbol}`.\n* It uses a fixed static catalog for the listed stocks (AAPL, MSFT, GOOGL, AMZN, NVDA).\n* Returns `HTTP 200` with the symbol and price, or `HTTP 400` if the symbol is unknown.\n* It remains completely independent of any database.\n\n### 2. `user-service`\n* Added `UserEntity` (with `cashBalance` defaulting to `10000.00`) and `HoldingEntity` targeting the local `user_db`.\n* Implemented `UserController` covering the public routes `POST /api/users` and `GET /api/users/{userId}/portfolio`. \n* Portfolio valuation is successfully calculated by fetching prices through a synchronous OpenFeign call to `market-service`.\n* Introduced an internal `InternalUserController` mapping to `/api/internal/users/*` which exposes isolated internal operations to check user existence and process `buy`/`sell` transaction updates.\n\n### 3. `trade-service`\n* Added `TradeEntity` targeting the local `trade_db`.\n* Implemented `TradeController` handling `POST /api/trades/buy`, `POST /api/trades/sell` and `GET /api/users/{userId}/trades`.\n* Orchestrates trades synchronously by:\n  1. Validating shares logic (`> 0`).\n  2. Retrieving real-time quotes using an OpenFeign client to `market-service`.\n  3. Attempting the financial operation on `user-service` through an OpenFeign client.\n  4. If both synchronous calls succeed, the trade is persisted locally to `trade_db`.\n* Configured `RabbitMQConfig` holding the required definitions. A successful trade persists its state and then sends an event message (with the exact `exchange`, `routing/event key` and `queue` required) using the `RabbitTemplate`.\n* Rejected trades gracefully return `HTTP 400` or `HTTP 404` based on conditions and prevent the transaction from being recorded locally or on RabbitMQ.\n\n### 4. `api-gateway`\n* Adjusted `api-gateway/src/main/resources/application.yml` to correct the `portfolio-service` route. It originally targeted `trade-service` but was corrected to forward `Path=/api/users/*/portfolio` to `lb://user-service` as `user-service` rightfully owns the user/portfolio state. \n* Left all public routes and properties structurally intact.\n\nI am confident in the implementation. The orchestration relies entirely on synchronous HTTP service-to-service communication avoiding distributed Saga frameworks or 2PC logic, while respecting strict microservices data segregation. You may proceed with the independent orchestration build and testing.\n",
